## Experience Mora

Mora is a legendary sports destination. Deeply rooted in outdoor tradition, Mora is the finish line for the historic [Vasaloppet](https://vasaloppet.se/en/), the world's oldest and biggest cross-country ski race, and [Cykelvasan](https://www.vasaloppet.se/en/summer/), one of Sweden's largest and most popular MTB races.

The event is organised by [IFK Mora Orienteering Club](https://www.svenskalag.se/ifkmora-ok), a club with extensive experience in hosting major international events in orienteering, MTBO, and Ski-O.

### Nature reserves for sports

The competitions will be held in two nature reserves, both unique because they are designated specifically for sports and recreation. One of them is the legendary Vasaloppet Arena, a nature reserve stretching almost 90 km long but just 20–30 metres wide—a historic track synonymous with Swedish endurance sports.

### The Dala Horse

{% FloatedImage
   src="~/assets/images/posts/wmtboc26/dala-horse-kids.jpg"
   alt="Dala Horse and Kids"
   float="right"
   cropPosition="center top"
   width="300px" /%}

Mora is synonymous with the Dala Horse (Dalahäst). The traditional wooden horses have been carved and painted in the villages around Mora since the 17th century. The [red horse](https://www.theswedishwoodenhorse.com/dala-horse-history) with its _kurbits_ painting is a national symbol of Sweden.

When you visit Mora, you are in the very heart of this tradition and you can find them everywhere.

## The Terrain

Forget what you know about Falun and its typical Swedish rocky trails and roots! The terrain for WMTBOC 2026 offers a completely different experience. We are heading to the pine forests and flowing trails and contours more similar to **Mora By (Säterbygden)**, the place where the Relay and Middle distance were held during the 2022 World Championships.

The terrain features fast riding, flowy trail networks and good visibility — pure MTBO enjoyment! See for yourself in these pictures:

