## Open Public Races

It's not just for the national teams! We are organising open races in conjunction with the World Championships. These races are part of the **Swedish Veteran Cup**.

Come and race on the same **high-quality maps** as the World Championships!

- **Note:** Public courses are unique and differ from the elite courses. This ensures you can fully enjoy the **Live stream and GPS tracking** of the elite races without having seen your course beforehand. No spoilers — just pure racing!

The registration for open public races is available on Swedish Eventor:

- [Public Race 1, Long Distance (28 Aug)](https://eventor.orientering.se/Events/Show/56226)
- [Public Race 2, Middle Distance (29 Aug)](https://eventor.orientering.se/Events/Show/56227)
- [Public Race 3, Sprint Distance (30 Aug)](https://eventor.orientering.se/Events/Show/56228)

![Full focus on reading the map before start](src/assets/images/posts/wmtboc26/mtbo_start.jpg)

## Plan your trip

**Getting Here:** Mora is easily accessible for international travellers via **Stockholm Arlanda Airport (ARN)**. From Arlanda, the journey to Mora takes approx. 3.5 – 4 hours. There are also direct flights available from Stockholm Arlanda to Mora operated by [Jonair](https://www.jonair.se).

**Travel tips:** While there is a direct train to Mora, please note that luggage space is limited and _bike bags are not guaranteed_ on board. To ensure smooth transport and save on rental costs, we recommend teams rent a _single van or large car_ at Arlanda to transport all bikes and heavy luggage.

This allows the athletes to take the comfortable direct train while limiting your fuel and rental expenses to just one vehicle.

**Accommodation:** The **Event Centre (EC)** is located at [Moraparken](https://en.firstcamp.se/destinations/moraparken-dalarna), a beautiful holiday resort by the river. It offers hotel rooms, cabins, and camping — everything you need in one place. Once you arrive, the event is largely car-free. Accommodations, competition areas and the Event Centre are within easy biking distance, so a daily vehicle is not required.

